{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1549970-what-do-u-think-of-ai-generated-artwork","id":1549970,"title":"What do u think of AI generated artwork?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-09T11:21:46-07:00","id":1549970,"title":"What do u think of AI generated artwork?","content":"I've seen that it can be good, but at times it looks to polished and it lacks that certain passion that you can see in other artwork where you can see the mistakes and or progression of a Alex Ross, Dale Kewon or Da Vinci. I'm not sure what I think about it.<br /> <br /> What do you people think about this technology?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T14:05:41-07:00","id":1549978,"title":"","content":"I've yet to see AI capable of producing something I recognize as art.<br /> <br /> I've seen some decent copy-algorithm generated images, but nothing that justifies the enormous costs involved (even if hidden from &quot;free users&quot; who aren't the actual customers and are just being used to normalize tech that shouldn't be normalized yet), the lack of compensation for humans that had their work used without permission to train those algorithms, the continued devaluation of human creativity so corporations can pump out slop until that's the only thing on the market at a reasonable price, and so on.<br /> <br /> If you want custom art you don't have the skills to make yourself, find an artist and pay them; art is good, we need to pay artists so they can keep making art, and you get something truly artistic and unique.<br /> <br /> If you want a pretty image for something, there are literally millions of free-to-use license stock images on the Internet that as a normal person trying to find something for their personal use to get you whatever you're after. The time it takes to learn how to find and search those databases isn't any harder or longer than becoming a good &quot;prompt writer.&quot;<br /> <br /> The only advantage to the algorithms is speed, but why rush if you want art?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T18:20:51-07:00","id":1549988,"title":"","content":"As a tool the AI has quite some promise, but there are still many problems.<br /> <br /> The sheer amount of resources is one of them. When you have companies thinking about building their own Nuclear Powerplants just to keep the AI working, that's telling of how far we still are from this being something we should be using so much.<br /> <br /> I personally don't blame the AI for the many concerns we should have with it. And we should have a lot. Art is just the tip of the iceberg. It has wonderful potential, but it will be used in the context of big companies doing what big companies do. It isn't good, it isn't pretty.<br /> <br /> But yeah, for now AI isn't yet capable of producing art. An AI generated image may be <i>turned</i> into art in some ways, but it isn't by itself. And it feeds from actual art being made by actual artists, that will keep existing to feed those algorithms, just with less pay and worse working conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T19:07:55-07:00","id":1549989,"title":"","content":"For now, AI art still has very obvious tells. Of course, AI art only started getting big a couple of years ago. In another decade or so it could reach a point where it's essentially indistinguishable from something made by a person without a very close examination. I think for the general masses, they won't really care if something they see (a poster, a picture in a book, an advertisement) was made by AI, as long as they can't spot any obvious flaws or differences.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of would-be-artists who might otherwise spend time practicing, refining and improving their artwork will instead rely entirely on AI to make art for them because it's a lot easier, but I guess going forward, artwork produced by human hands will be much more special because it will be comparatively rarer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T20:06:02-07:00","id":1549991,"title":"","content":"The problem for these sorts of learning models, is that they can't be creative. They can only approximate creativity by mixing up stuff humans made and humans feed into the algorithm.<br /> <br /> Since the people feeding the machines don't want to pay the humans making the art (seriously, there was a recent court hearing where some of the big companies in this space argued that they should be completely exempt from having to obey copyright laws), the people making the art are just going to make it harder and harder to access digitally. Once there's no new art to feed to the computers, we know what happens: the quality drops immensely. The quality of the outputs directly depends on the quality of the inputs (as in human art, not prompts), and once the inputs are just past outputs, the systems quickly iterate themselves into nonsense*.<br /> <br /> Learning models will eventually lose without human artists. The question is whether society makes sure there's skilled human artists around once the bubble bursts.<br /> <br /> * edit: this is the fundamental case that what we have computers doing isn't art. Human arts do learn by copying older art as well, but that's to study and refine techniques and mastery over things like materials. Human artists will get to a point where at worst their skills plateau, but they aren't going to degrade if they can't see other artists' work to copy it for ideas. They have their own creative ideas to express. The algorithms can't do that. The current systems in question aren't mastering skills in order to express original ideas. They're just remixing existing expressions, and when you take those expressions away, there's nothing to remix, and there's no original ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 04-09-2025, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-09T11:37:42-07:00","id":1558751,"title":"","content":"<b>It's dog shit.</b><br /> <br /> Not only does AI art come off as way too glossy and plastic, but they all look like they're made by the same artist, because THEY ARE.<br /> <br /> People who use AI programs just type in a prompt, let the computer do the bulk of the heavy lifting, and then if they have any degree of technical skill, they might deign to make some edits. Before uploading it and claiming its their own creation.<br /> <br /> AI programs are trained by feeding them information from previously existing sources. Well, those sources are often generated by humans; except that human artists are quitting the profession, because AI is stealing all their jobs.<br /> <br /> Which means these AI's will inevitably begin copying each other, leading to copies of the copies of the copies.<br /> <br /> You know what happens when you try to clone a clone, right? It becomes progressively worse with each generation!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-09T12:44:10-07:00","id":1558753,"title":"","content":"Well, fortunately in the US at least, the courts have ruled that algorithmically generated content doesn't get copyright protections. So you can claim a picture it &quot;yours&quot; all you want, but regardless of if you're a person playing with a fun digital toy, or a major corporation, the second you post the content anywhere it's instantly either the original IP owner's property or public domain (not entirely clear but it doesn't really matter for the future of trying to turn these things into an industry).<br /> <br /> While there's going to be a lot of litigation left around how much human hands need to be involved for something to qualify for IP protections (aka something corporations can actually profit from), it is a big brake in the creative industries on trying to automate everything. They're going to need actual human artists - not just prompt writers - if they actually want to own their outputs to sell them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-09T15:05:57-07:00","id":1558757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1549970-what-do-u-think-of-ai-generated-artwork?p=1558753#post1558753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, fortunately in the US at least, the courts have ruled that algorithmically generated content doesn't get copyright protections. So you can claim a picture it &quot;yours&quot; all you want, but regardless of if you're a person playing with a fun digital toy, or a major corporation, the second you post the content anywhere it's instantly either the original IP owner's property or public domain (not entirely clear but it doesn't really matter for the future of trying to turn these things into an industry).<br /> <br /> While there's going to be a lot of litigation left around how much human hands need to be involved for something to qualify for IP protections (aka something corporations can actually profit from), it is a big brake in the creative industries on trying to automate everything. They're going to need actual human artists - not just prompt writers - if they actually want to own their outputs to sell them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using AI for art is also the least of our worries when it comes to this new age of technology.<br /> <br /> If the program that is specifically designed to recreate whatever pictures you feed it is still failing basic anatomy lessons, I really do not trust them to design one that's put in charge of guiding medical procedures.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, the collapse of that AI bubble may be happening faster than I expected. Seems like Microsoft did the stupid move of putting all their eggs in one basket and expecting their partners to jump on board the AI train. Only for them to decide they either weren't ready for such a radical change, or didn't trust it enough, so they're sticking with Windows 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-09T15:38:53-07:00","id":1558759,"title":"","content":"Considering the recent case would mean that things like video games or even just general apps that are found to be coded by algorithms instead of primarily by humans wouldn't be protected from other people just copying it for themselves instead of paying for it, that's a lot of money in the tech world that wouldn't be going to shareholders if companies over-push such coding. Copyright and IP protections aren't just about art (and really have never just been about art, it's always been about who gets to profit off of creative work that isn't limited to art specifically).<br /> <br /> Also overbroad Copilot integration is just one of many, many, many issues that major corporate and power-user customers of Windows have with Windows 11. The Windows 10 holdouts have already become a drop in the bucket for future sales; Microsoft's real damage control issue people looking to swap to Linux forks over Windows 11 because it's easier for major customers to maintain backwards compatibility and install on older systems with some of the Linux forks than it is with Windows 11... which is an entirely different level of dumb from Microsoft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-09T18:14:49-07:00","id":1558763,"title":"","content":"I for one, welcome our new AI-Overlords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-09T19:57:04-07:00","id":1558765,"title":"","content":"Except we're not getting AI-Overlords, we're getting AI-middle-managers that make the uber-rich richer and screw everyone else even harder than how things have already been going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-10T14:15:04-07:00","id":1558776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1549970-what-do-u-think-of-ai-generated-artwork?p=1558763#post1558763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I for one, welcome our new AI-Overlords.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll be waiting a long while, because these are just an auto-complete function that has too much power supplied to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-10T19:00:44-07:00","id":1558781,"title":"","content":"So coming back to this, I will say AI artwork is nice for certain minor things. Like playing video games where you can insert your own character portrait (I'm playing through Wrath of the Righteous at the moment), it's nice being able to use AI to generate a portrait that perfectly fits your character concept rather than having to dig through thousands of pictures to try and find something similar to what you're thinking. Likewise, its nice for quickly creating visuals for an RPG session where you wouldn't want to spend the time or money on to get visuals the traditional way, especially given that those visuals will likely be one-offs and never get used again. <br /> <br /> So basically, it's nice for stuff that doesn't actually matter much and isn't going to have any permanent significance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T18:02:08-07:00","id":1558812,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Onyx Path has a strict policy against AI. Please do not post it in our spaces. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T18:40:59-07:00","id":1559003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1549970-what-do-u-think-of-ai-generated-artwork?p=1558776#post1558776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'll be waiting a long while, because these are just an auto-complete function that has too much power supplied to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And a lot of investors with too much money and little understand of what AI actually is. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T18:52:26-07:00","id":1559004,"title":"","content":"And AI is great for creating a character-image, but, it's kinda lame when all you do is type, &quot;Two Werewolves fighting in the woods&quot;. And AI images have to match the game your playing. A realistic image of a person for a CoD game? When most of the art in the books are sketches? No. Maybe for D&amp;D 5th edition, if it looks cartoonish, maybe. That's why I like Heromachine; I can do a black&amp;white, character, and it looks, Cyberpunk or WoD. I also can colorize them as well. <br /> <br /> My favorite program for making character was Flashface.de. It was like a police sketch-program; then, some guy bought it and turned it into an Android-App, and I couldn't use it. ARG! <br /> <br /> AI is a hole; because, a good idea is a good idea; I used an older program, that randomly creates planetary-maps; it produced a highland region, and then I realized I had a massive volcano, the size of a continent and it got me thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-06T11:41:51-07:00","id":1559251,"title":"","content":"There is an art to ai generated artwork, it's the art of communication as it can only work with what information you give it. There's a YouTuber who dresses up as Skeletor and he did a couple of videos on the topic on how it will not be replacing actual artists anytime soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-06T14:21:12-07:00","id":1559254,"title":"","content":"I have to wonder if these people have ever actually commissioned art from humans before... everyone keeps talking about this being some new fancy &quot;art&quot; to learn to do prompts effectively... but being good at communication has always been part of having art done for you if you're not going to learn how to do it yourself. The nice thing about humans, is you can have conversations with them because, you know, they're thinking minds instead of algorithms, where they can tell you if you need to be more specific about something, if you're comfortable with them taking creative liberties, etc. <br /> <br /> Prompting writing isn't a new skill. It's a highly narrowed down version of a very old skill (communication) that loses out of the ability to learn a lot of things in the process beyond how to get a machine to spit out what you're looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-06T18:38:03-07:00","id":1559260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1549970-what-do-u-think-of-ai-generated-artwork?p=1559254#post1559254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to wonder if these people have ever actually commissioned art from humans before... everyone keeps talking about this being some new fancy &quot;art&quot; to learn to do prompts effectively... but being good at communication has always been part of having art done for you if you're not going to learn how to do it yourself. The nice thing about humans, is you can have conversations with them because, you know, they're thinking minds instead of algorithms, where they can tell you if you need to be more specific about something, if you're comfortable with them taking creative liberties, etc.<br /> <br /> Prompting writing isn't a new skill. It's a highly narrowed down version of a very old skill (communication) that loses out of the ability to learn a lot of things in the process beyond how to get a machine to spit out what you're looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact people actually believe stringing together a bunch of key words and then spinning the RNG wheel, until the computer gives you something close to what you wanted is a new form of &quot;art&quot; just goes to show how <b>creatively bankrupt</b> this generation is.<br /> <br /> My god, people are lazy as fuck these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-06T20:39:22-07:00","id":1559264,"title":"","content":"I don't see it as a strictly generational thing. Lots of the AI hype is coming from older people. A lot of Baby Boomers I know love the ability to make some quick cutesy thing to add to a social media post or email or whatever; even if they're a bit more conscious of it being a new fangled toy instead of treating it like the great new future of everything. A lot of the most ardent anti-AI folks I know are Zoomers and Gen Alpha because they can see this is just another straw being tossed on the back of a camel that already collapsed from exhaustion a few thousand straws ago.<br /> <br /> Everyone, from every generation, is as lazy as life lets them be. Gen X was also labeled the slacker generation over two decades ago.<br /> <br /> The thing is, is that people want their work to feel proportional to the perceived value of the results. This cuts both ways though. It's a great instinct for avoiding undervaluing yourself or falling for scams. But at the same time greedy people love to manipulate perceived value to manipulate the work expectations for things. A bunch of money-brain addled corpos want to use these tools to make the perceived value of art lower. For five minutes of free playing around with a website you can make a cute greeting card that you'd have to drive to the store and pay a few bucks for; and you can personalize it. It's just that the real costs are trying to be hidden as much as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-07T01:00:53-07:00","id":1559267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1549970-what-do-u-think-of-ai-generated-artwork?p=1559264#post1559264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see it as a strictly generational thing. Lots of the AI hype is coming from older people. A lot of Baby Boomers I know love the ability to make some quick cutesy thing to add to a social media post or email or whatever; even if they're a bit more conscious of it being a new fangled toy instead of treating it like the great new future of everything. A lot of the most ardent anti-AI folks I know are Zoomers and Gen Alpha because they can see this is just another straw being tossed on the back of a camel that already collapsed from exhaustion a few thousand straws ago.<br /> <br /> Everyone, from every generation, is as lazy as life lets them be. Gen X was also labeled the slacker generation over two decades ago.<br /> <br /> The thing is, is that people want their work to feel proportional to the perceived value of the results. This cuts both ways though. It's a great instinct for avoiding undervaluing yourself or falling for scams. But at the same time greedy people love to manipulate perceived value to manipulate the work expectations for things. A bunch of money-brain addled corpos want to use these tools to make the perceived value of art lower. For five minutes of free playing around with a website you can make a cute greeting card that you'd have to drive to the store and pay a few bucks for; and you can personalize it. It's just that the real costs are trying to be hidden as much as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sick of clicking on a video and being presented with an either monotone voice, or a computer that's making a cringe attempt at being cheerful and friendly, only to have them routinely change how they pronounce the same words. Along with a slideshow of background images that commonly appear warped and misshapen.<br /> <br /> Like, I concede that not everybody has the skills to perform correctional edits to artwork, but at the very least you can do your own voice overs!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-07T03:45:23-07:00","id":1559270,"title":"","content":"Imagine what it's like for creators that have to use text-to-speech software just to have a voice in their videos, and spend huge amounts of money on high quality vocals that let them have a unique aural personality that they can't from their own throat... only to have to compete with that slop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-08T03:22:23-07:00","id":1559287,"title":"","content":"Or have problems with verbal communication and this is great tool to aid them and you get lumped in with low quality users.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-08T15:04:43-07:00","id":1559295,"title":"","content":"I tried to frame my post widely to a number of potential reasons, but IME people that simply struggle with verbal communication doing pre-recorded videos don't opt for high end TTS (or STTS) setups. All of the steps to create your own digital voice, a custom computer that exists to process that voice fast enough to keep up with a live-chat or live-stream, and so on is a lot compared to maybe needing a few more takes than average for a video creator. That's why I focused on those that need the assistive tech; though need can be more than a physical impairment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-10T19:56:23-07:00","id":1559336,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I can tell a vid's AI when it pronounces things wrong; however, if I were to produce an educational-video, I'd straight up use an accredited textbook and use text-to-voice because, I'm not a geologist or historian and I'd rather have the experts speak than me. I don't like misinformation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T21:34:59-07:00","id":1560924,"title":"","content":"I really wish there was a clear delineation between cloud based AI generated artwork and locally generated artwork. This is especially important to me because I have a degree in computer science and built my own system from the ground up. I trained it on my own art, my friends artwork (with their permission), and public domain art.<br /> <br /> It is frustrating to see local AI generation lumped in with cloud based AI and banned everywhere under broad AI bans. There should be a separate case for locally run models especially since many of us give them away for free.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T00:21:11-07:00","id":1560927,"title":"","content":"How is anyone else supposed to know if you're using a truly ethically trained local model vs. slapping some custom interfaces over an existing large model?<br /> <br /> This is part of the problem with the past decade or so of &quot;move fast and break things,&quot; that has been dominating the tech industry. There's no consideration for public responses, establishing protocols and standards, and so on. The strength of the negative responses to gen models of any size is spurned by the big companies trying to shove it into every part of our lives so they can justify the vast amount of resources invested into the tech (since the tech itself repeatedly proves that it's nowhere near a state to be a functional tool in 99% of idealized commercial use cases).<br /> <br /> With no infrastructure for consumer protections to adequately certify model training sources and so on, the general public is forced to simply assume; some people are going to assume positively, and some negatively based on their concerns and tolerances. At the moment the only option is blind trust... and depending on the target demographic that could be fairly easy to ask (South Koreans poll highly towards assuming good intentions for implementing models) or nearly impossible (North America and Europe are generally the complete opposite). But that also trends towards who's mostly exposed to the costs of the &quot;move fast and break things&quot; mantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T10:27:26-07:00","id":1560937,"title":"","content":"Youtube just started trying to advertise me with an E-Girl companion... for &quot;late night gaming,&quot; as they called it.<br /> <br /> Seriously, fuck AI generated content. I will not be called maidenless by a fucking Alexa!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T19:24:25-07:00","id":1561213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1549970-what-do-u-think-of-ai-generated-artwork?p=1559251#post1559251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is an art to ai generated artwork, it's the art of communication as it can only work with what information you give it. There's a YouTuber who dresses up as Skeletor and he did a couple of videos on the topic on how it will not be replacing actual artists anytime soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen that video by CKY too. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T15:10:21-07:00","id":1561849,"title":"","content":"I get really pissed with flat statements like &quot;there's no art to string of words&quot; by people who doesn't know the scene and how varied it is. A good AI generated image requires a lot of work beyond communication.<br /> <br /> Hence why so much slop <i>isn't</i> good. You have to dig a lot to find most good works.<br /> <br /> All that said, I'm joining the anti-AI crowd on most of this. Heavy Arms said a lot of truths here.<br /> <br /> The AI won't ever substitute artists. But this is not the problem. Companies use it to drive down the price of artistic work. To pay less for professionals they still need and are still as skilled and highly trained as before. Worst case scenario of an illustrator still asking for the usual fee, you change the name to &quot;AI asset assistant&quot; or some shit and demand the same work for a third of the price or less.<br /> <br /> We need to reign in this tide. Not the tech itself, but the companies that get to do whatever with no accountability. The challenge almost isn't technical, either, it's mostly regulation and politics. Tracking the image post-production to always know what's AI and who made it isn't hard. Making training data auditable is feasible and defining adequate rules for Trademark and Copyright for AI Output is a matter of political will.<br /> <br /> No AI output should be permitted commercial or public use. If you want to sell or upload to YouTube or TikTok, pay an artist. Any worker who deals with AI at any stage of production must be trained and paid as a professional, to both ensure quality and that you're not just hiding bad labor practices.<br /> <br /> Even if better practices don't eliminate all problems, they can reduce them to usual rates of problems and we improve from there, but we must get there first.<br /> <br /> Some generators in the internet pay the artists who trained them. Outside those, if that much, my firm position is: don't pay for AI generators, don't give your data to access AI generators. If you can, avoid cloud generators at all, while it's not exactly easy to run one locally, it's less hard that before. Use them for yourself, for minor things you wouldn't pay for anyway and to learn.<br /> <br /> For media platforms: if you notice a video is AI, stop it. The algorithm measures how long you stay, that's the most important metric. Use an ad block, consider disabling it for videos you want to monetize, keep it on for everything else especially before being sure it's not AI. Or leave the official apps at all, there are alternative apps for the same platforms that bypass their main system and keep your data out of Google's grubby hands. You won't get rid of them completely, but you can harm their goals profoundly.<br /> <br /> Only thing I'll say regarding those who use TTS: there are many ways someone can be disabled for communication besides physical problems. I'll probably use if I come to make videos, since I'm Autistic and yes, I'd fare worse than the AI. I can actually edit and stuff and improve, but I won't expose myself to actual neurological just because someone else wants to say what kind of assistive tech I deserve. Not pointing fingers, just want that to be very clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T15:31:47-07:00","id":1561850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1549970-what-do-u-think-of-ai-generated-artwork?p=1561849#post1561849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The AI won't ever substitute artists. But this is not the problem. Companies use it to drive down the price of artistic work. To pay less for professionals they still need and are still as skilled and highly trained as before. Worst case scenario of an illustrator still asking for the usual fee, you change the name to &quot;AI asset assistant&quot; or some shit and demand the same work for a third of the price or less.<br /> <br /> We need to reign in this tide. Not the tech itself, but the companies that get to do whatever with no accountability. The challenge almost isn't technical, either, it's mostly regulation and politics. Tracking the image post-production to always know what's AI and who made it isn't hard. Making training data auditable is feasible and defining adequate rules for Trademark and Copyright for AI Output is a matter of political will.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Once you've seen enough of it, you start to realize there are certain tells that make it easy to identity.<br /> <br /> First and foremost, closely examine the hands and feet. That's one of the major giveaways. After that, check the image background for any distortions.<br /> <br /> Lastly that comes to mind, is if the artwork appears too be made of plastic / rubber, or if it has a glossy / shiny design to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1549970-what-do-u-think-of-ai-generated-artwork?p=1561849#post1561849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For media platforms: if you notice a video is AI, stop it. The algorithm measures how long you stay, that's the most important metric. Use an ad block, consider disabling it for videos you want to monetize, keep it on for everything else especially before being sure it's not AI. Or leave the official apps at all, there are alternative apps for the same platforms that bypass their main system and keep your data out of Google's grubby hands. You won't get rid of them completely, but you can harm their goals profoundly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've taken to immediately muting any ads that pop up, and waiting for the SKIP button to appear. I suppose that doesn't change the view length, but it grants me peace of mind knowing that I have the power to silence the AI slop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T15:48:38-07:00","id":1561854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1549970-what-do-u-think-of-ai-generated-artwork?p=1561850#post1561850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once you've seen enough of it, you start to realize there are certain tells that make it easy to identity.<br /> <br /> First and foremost, closely examine the hands and feet. That's one of the major giveaways. After that, check the image background for any distortions.<br /> <br /> Lastly that comes to mind, is if the artwork appears too be made of plastic / rubber, or if it has a glossy / shiny design to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I've taken to immediately muting any ads that pop up, and waiting for the SKIP button to appear. I suppose that doesn't change the view length, but it grants me peace of mind knowing that I have the power to silence the AI slop.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem isn't you being able to identify. For now that's easy.<br /> <br /> But no one should be required to try, to begin with. Also no company should be granted any plausible deniability. Finally, deep fakes and images that constitute crimes must be tracked to the person who generated and spread.<br /> <br /> I don't think <i>generating</i> should be illegal, but when you publicize it you must be dealt with.<br /> <br /> For ads: muting does nothing, skipping does little, and watching to the end feeds the algorithm. Not watching is actually the most important part, as it diminishes how much others will be exposed to that crap. For ads the ideal is still an ad block.<br /> <br /> Usually I don't recommend or use ad blocks as I won't to actually help the content creator, but if it's something I don't want to finance, I won't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T17:17:49-07:00","id":1561858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1549970-what-do-u-think-of-ai-generated-artwork?p=1561854#post1561854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem isn't you being able to identify. For now that's easy.<br /> <br /> But no one should be required to try, to begin with. Also no company should be granted any plausible deniability. Finally, deep fakes and images that constitute crimes must be tracked to the person who generated and spread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. But for now, I'm reminding myself about the existence of Auto Tune, and how widespread that became in the entertainment industry.<br /> <br /> It ultimately turned out to be a passing fad, and that's hopefully what will happen here too. Once people get bored with it.<br /> <br /> I've noticed that AI Dagoth Ur and Presidents Play seem to have fizzled out in popularity over the last few years.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1549970-what-do-u-think-of-ai-generated-artwork?p=1561854#post1561854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For ads: muting does nothing, skipping does little, and watching to the end feeds the algorithm. Not watching is actually the most important part, as it diminishes how much others will be exposed to that crap. For ads the ideal is still an ad block.<br /> <br /> Usually I don't recommend or use ad blocks as I won't to actually help the content creator, but if it's something I don't want to finance, I won't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got Adblock Plus on two computers, and for some reason, it only seems to work on one of them. My gaming computer plays ads on Youtube, regardless of how many times Adblock updates itself. While on my basic computer, it blocks the ads just fine.<br /> <br /> I don't know what the difference is between them, so I don't know why one works correctly and the other doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}